town University School of Law. Founders were William O. Moore and George 6. Hurley, State University of Iowa; Kenneth E. Oberholtzer, University of Illinois; Dean William A. Hamilton, College of William and Mary; Russell D. Tubaugh, Ohio University; Paul A. Lomax, University of Southern California; William Waldo Girdner, George Washington University; and Carl E. Anderson, University of Minnesota. It was a founding member of the Professional Interfraternity Conference\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0259-8b82a959c277:d01\", \"text\": \"Phi Delta Gamma (social) Phi Delta Gamma (ΦΔΓ) of Puerto Rico is the first Puerto Rican organization of Greek letters, which was founded in the western town of Mayagüez,on April 25, 1942. Phi Delta Gamma originated from a high school fraternity, Alpha Iota Omega, which was founded in 1939. When the brothers of Alpha Iota Omega enrolled in the College of Agriculture and Mechanic Arts (Colegio de Agricultura y Artes Mecánicas) of Mayagüez, some were offered the opportunity to pledge one of the original Puerto Rican fraternities. The others reunited in the house of the brothers Gilberto Oliver Padilla and\"}], \"fallible_prior\": [\"1876\"], \"prior_explanation\": \"Phi Delta Gamma was founded in 1876 at Monmouth College (now Monmouth University).\", \"fallible_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0259-8b82a959c277:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0259-8b82a959c277:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"Phi Delta Gamma\", \"scope\": \"founded\", \"claim\": \"Phi Delta Gamma was founded on June 7, 1924.\", \"answer\": \"June 7, 1924\", \"quote\": \"Phi Delta Gamma was founded on June 7, 1924 at the University of Iowa at Georgetown University School of Law.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0259-8b82a959c277:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0259-8b82a959c277:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"Phi Delta Gamma\", \"scope\": \"founded\", \"claim\": \"Phi Delta Gamma was founded on April 25, 1942.\", \"answer\": \"April 25, 1942\", \"quote\": \"Phi Delta Gamma (social) Phi Delta Gamma (ΦΔΓ) of Puerto Rico is the first Puerto Rican organization of Greek letters, which was founded in the western town of Mayagüez,on April 25, 1942.\", \"original_document_number\": 2}], \"fallible_previous_answer\": [\"June 7, 1924\", \"April 25, 1942\"]}"
